DTEND:20261209T172000Z
SUMMARY:Dulles: 52-minute connection
LOCATION:Washington Dulles (IAD)
DESCRIPTION:No customs here. Walk or take the AeroTrain to the UA 803 gate
 . Look up the gate in the app before landing.\nThe long day
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d-1-3@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261209T172000Z
DTEND:20261210T075000Z
SUMMARY:UA 803 Dulles → Haneda
DESCRIPTION:Boeing 777-200\, 14 h 30. Stay awake for the first half\, slee
 p the second half. Lands 16:50 Japan time on Thu Dec 10.\nThe long day
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Boarding soon: UA 803 Dulles → Haneda
TRIGGER:-PT75M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d1-0@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261210T075000Z
DTEND:20261210T090000Z
SUMMARY:Land at Haneda Terminal 3
LOCATION:Haneda Airport Terminal 3
DESCRIPTION:Immigration and customs with your Visit Japan Web QR codes; al
 low 45–75 min. Pull ¥30\,000 each from the 7-Bank ATM in arrivals.\nDa
 y 1: Land\, eat\, soak\, sleep
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d1-1@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261210T090000Z
DTEND:20261210T101500Z
SUMMARY:Suica\, then into the city
DESCRIPTION:Moziah and AJ: Suica in Apple Wallet. Trenton: try adding Suic
 a to Google Wallet; global Pixels usually can't\, so buy a Welcome Suica 
 card at T3. Then the Limousine Bus (≈ ¥1\,400) or Keikyū + JR (≈ ¥
 550).\n≈ ¥550–1\,400\nDay 1: Land\, eat\, soak\, sleep
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d1-2@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261210T101500Z
DTEND:20261210T110000Z
SUMMARY:Check in at Hotel Gracery Shinjuku
LOCATION:Hotel Gracery Shinjuku
DESCRIPTION:Lobby on 8F of the Godzilla-head building. Drop bags.\nDay 1: 
 Land\, eat\, soak\, sleep
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d1-3@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261210T110000Z
DTEND:20261210T121500Z
SUMMARY:Shinjuku Kabuki Hall
LOCATION:Shinjuku Kabuki Hall
DESCRIPTION:New for you: a loud\, neon\, festival-themed food hall on 2F o
 f the Tokyu Kabukichō Tower\, two minutes from the hotel. Ten stalls of 
 regional food: Hokkaido yakitori\, Kyushu spicy noodles\, Korean barbecue
 . Open most of the night.\n≈ ¥3\,000–4\,500\nDay 1: Land\, eat\, soa
 k\, sleep
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d1-4@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261210T121500Z
DTEND:20261210T134500Z
SUMMARY:Thermae-Yu hot spring
LOCATION:Thermae-Yu
DESCRIPTION:New for you: a hot-spring bathhouse 5 min from the hotel. Outd
 oor bath\, carbonated bath\, two saunas. Be out before midnight\, when a 
 late-night surcharge starts. No tattoos. Bed by 23:00.\n¥3\,100 (Mon–T
 hu rate)\nDay 1: Land\, eat\, soak\, sleep
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-0@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T000000Z
DTEND:20261211T004500Z
SUMMARY:Train to Sakuragichō
DESCRIPTION:JR Shōnan-Shinjuku Line to Yokohama\, then one stop on the Ne
 gishi Line.\n≈ ¥600–700\nDay 2: Yokohama: noodles\, harbour\, Chinat
 own\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-1@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T004500Z
DTEND:20261211T010000Z
SUMMARY:Yokohama Air Cabin
LOCATION:Yokohama Air Cabin
DESCRIPTION:A gondola from Sakuragichō Station over the harbour to the Sh
 inkō pier\, 5 min. One cabin fits the three of you.\n¥1\,000\nDay 2: Yo
 kohama: noodles\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-2@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T010000Z
DTEND:20261211T030000Z
SUMMARY:Cup Noodles Museum
LOCATION:Cup Noodles Museum Yokohama
DESCRIPTION:Take a numbered ticket for the My Cupnoodles Factory as you wa
 lk in: draw on your own cup\, pick the soup and four toppings\, take it h
 ome sealed. Open 10:00–18:00. Allow 90 min.\n¥500 entry · ¥500 your 
 cup\nDay 2: Yokohama: noodles\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-3@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T030000Z
DTEND:20261211T044500Z
SUMMARY:Red Brick Warehouse Christmas Market
LOCATION:Yokohama Red Brick Warehouse
DESCRIPTION:Runs Nov 20 – Dec 25. About 60 stalls\, an 11 m real tree\, 
 mulled wine and sausages with the harbour behind. First lunch. Check the 
 hours that week.\nentry from ¥500 · food ≈ ¥1\,500–2\,500\nDay 2: 
 Yokohama: noodles\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-4@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T044500Z
DTEND:20261211T064500Z
SUMMARY:Yamashita Park → Chinatown
LOCATION:Yokohama Chinatown
DESCRIPTION:Walk the waterfront (20 min) to Japan's biggest Chinatown. Sec
 ond lunch on foot: pork buns\, soup dumplings\, sesame balls.\n≈ ¥1\,5
 00–2\,500\nDay 2: Yokohama: noodles\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-5@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T064500Z
DTEND:20261211T090000Z
SUMMARY:Sunset from Ōsanbashi Pier
LOCATION:Ōsanbashi Pier
DESCRIPTION:A wooden rooftop deck with the whole Minato Mirai skyline acro
 ss the water\, and Mt Fuji behind it on a clear day. From 17:00 the Yorun
 oyo harbour light show runs every half hour.\nfree\nDay 2: Yokohama: nood
 les\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-6@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T090000Z
DTEND:20261211T120000Z
SUMMARY:Noge bar-hopping
LOCATION:Noge
DESCRIPTION:About 600 small bars and izakaya in a few blocks by Sakuragich
 ō\, mostly locals. Start at a standing bar\, then the curved two-storey 
 Miyakobashi "Harmonica Alley" on the river.\n≈ ¥4\,000–6\,000\nDay 2
 : Yokohama: noodles\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d2-7@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261211T140000Z
DTEND:20261211T153000Z
SUMMARY:Train back to Shinjuku
DESCRIPTION:From Sakuragichō. Don't push it: a taxi from Yokohama to Shin
 juku is ≈ ¥12\,000–15\,000.\n≈ ¥600–700\nDay 2: Yokohama: noodl
 es\, harbour\, Chinatown\, Noge
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Leave in 20 min: Train back to Shinjuku
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-0@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T003000Z
DTEND:20261212T013000Z
SUMMARY:Ship suitcases to Niseko
DESCRIPTION:Yamato takkyūbin from the front desk to the Mercure Niseko Re
 sort. Tokyo → Hokkaido takes 2 days\, so they land Dec 14\, ahead of yo
 u. Keep a daypack with 3 days of clothes\, onsen kit and warm layers.\n
 ≈ ¥3\,000–3\,700 per bag\nDay 3: Send the bags\, ski shops\, monjaya
 ki\, Ebisu
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Ship suitcases to Niseko
TRIGGER:-PT10M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-1@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T013000Z
DTEND:20261212T040000Z
SUMMARY:Ueno → Ameyoko
LOCATION:Ameyoko
DESCRIPTION:JR Yamanote\, Shinjuku → Ueno\, 25 min. Market street under 
 the tracks: street food\, sneakers\, cheap sashimi bowls\, standing bars 
 open from late morning.\ntrain ≈ ¥210–230 · food ≈ ¥1\,500–2\,
 500\nDay 3: Send the bags\, ski shops\, monjayaki\, Ebisu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-2@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T040000Z
DTEND:20261212T070000Z
SUMMARY:Kanda-Ogawamachi ski street
LOCATION:Kanda Ogawamachi ski shops
DESCRIPTION:JR to Ochanomizu (2 stops)\, then 5 min walk. About 60 ski and
  board shops in 400 m: gloves\, goggles and base layers before Niseko\, a
 nd Trenton's boot hunt. Tax refunds now happen at the airport.\nDay 3: Se
 nd the bags\, ski shops\, monjayaki\, Ebisu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-3@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T073000Z
DTEND:20261212T090000Z
SUMMARY:Marunouchi illuminations
LOCATION:Marunouchi Naka-dori
DESCRIPTION:One stop to Tokyo Station\, then walk Naka-dōri under the lit
  trees. The restored station building is lit too.\nfree\nDay 3: Send the 
 bags\, ski shops\, monjayaki\, Ebisu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-4@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T090000Z
DTEND:20261212T113000Z
SUMMARY:Monjayaki on Tsukishima Monja Street
LOCATION:Tsukishima Monja Street
DESCRIPTION:Yūrakuchō Line\, Yūrakuchō → Tsukishima\, 5 min. Tokyo's
  own runny\, crispy-edged griddle pancake: you cook it at the table and e
 at it off tiny spatulas. Dozens of shops on one street.\n≈ ¥2\,500–4
 \,000\nDay 3: Send the bags\, ski shops\, monjayaki\, Ebisu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-5@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T113000Z
DTEND:20261212T143000Z
SUMMARY:Ebisu Yokochō and Ebisu bars
LOCATION:Ebisu Yokochō
DESCRIPTION:Ōedo Line to Roppongi\, Hibiya Line to Ebisu\, 25 min. A cove
 red alley of loud\, friendly counters\, then the bars around the station.
 \n≈ ¥3\,000–5\,000\nDay 3: Send the bags\, ski shops\, monjayaki\, E
 bisu
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d3-6@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T151500Z
DTEND:20261212T164500Z
SUMMARY:Last trains · pack tonight
DESCRIPTION:Last trains about 00:15–00:45. Tomorrow you check out at 07:
 45: pack the daypack before you go out\, not after.\nDay 3: Send the bags
 \, ski shops\, monjayaki\, Ebisu
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Last trains leave in about 30 min
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
