DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261212T233000Z
DTEND:20261213T011500Z
SUMMARY:Hokuriku Shinkansen → Nagano
DESCRIPTION:Buy an ekiben (station bento) for breakfast on board. Sit on t
 he left for mountain views past Takasaki.\n¥8\,340 · bento ≈ ¥1\,200
 \nDay 4: Monkeys in the hot spring\, then your own
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Leave in 20 min: Hokuriku Shinkansen → Nagano
TRIGGER:-PT20M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-3@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T011500Z
DTEND:20261213T023000Z
SUMMARY:Nagano → Yudanaka
DESCRIPTION:Down to the Nagaden station. Buy the Snow Monkey Pass (train /
  local bus version): Nagaden for the day\, the bus to the park and back\,
  and park entry. Or pay as you go.\npass ¥5\,100\nDay 4: Monkeys in the 
 hot spring\, then your own
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-4@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T023000Z
DTEND:20261213T040000Z
SUMMARY:Drop bags\, soba lunch
LOCATION:Kanaguya
DESCRIPTION:Bags at the ryokan\, then soba or a set meal in Shibu.\n≈ ¥
 1\,200–1\,800\nDay 4: Monkeys in the hot spring\, then your own
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-5@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T040000Z
DTEND:20261213T044500Z
SUMMARY:Bus + forest trail to the park
DESCRIPTION:Local bus to the Snow Monkey Park stop (15 min)\, then a 1.6 k
 m trail\, 30–35 min each way\, often icy. Boots with grip; the trailhea
 d shop rents boots and sells slip-on spikes.\nbus in pass\nDay 4: Monkeys
  in the hot spring\, then your own
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Leave in 20 min: Bus + forest trail to the park
TRIGGER:-PT20M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-6@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T044500Z
DTEND:20261213T061500Z
SUMMARY:Jigokudani Monkey Park
LOCATION:Jigokudani Monkey Park
DESCRIPTION:Wild macaques around and in a steaming pool. Show your dated w
 eb-ticket QR. No food\, no flash\, no selfie sticks\, stay 1–2 m back. 
 Winter hours end at 16:00.\n¥1\,000 (from Dec 1)\nDay 4: Monkeys in the 
 hot spring\, then your own
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-7@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T061500Z
DTEND:20261213T070000Z
SUMMARY:Walk out\, bus back to Shibu
DESCRIPTION:Day 4: Monkeys in the hot spring\, then your own
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-8@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T070000Z
DTEND:20261213T090000Z
SUMMARY:Yukata\, bath key\, nine-bath circuit
DESCRIPTION:Check in\, change into yukata\, get the bath key and start the
  kyūtō-meguri. The baths are small and very hot; you won't do all nine 
 before dinner. Stamp card is in this app.\nfree for guests\nDay 4: Monkey
 s in the hot spring\, then your own
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-9@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T090000Z
DTEND:20261213T110000Z
SUMMARY:Kaiseki dinner
DESCRIPTION:Ten or so small courses\, usually with Shinshū beef\, river f
 ish and local sake.\nincluded\nDay 4: Monkeys in the hot spring\, then yo
 ur own
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jt26-d4-10@japan26-trip
DTSTAMP:20261113T175817Z
DTSTART:20261213T110000Z
DTEND:20261213T123000Z
SUMMARY:More baths\, lanterns\, sake
DESCRIPTION:The lantern-lit lane\, sake\, and the retro shooting gallery i
 f it's open. Futons get laid out while you eat. Public baths close at 22:
 00.\nsake ≈ ¥800 a glass\nDay 4: Monkeys in the hot spring\, then your
  own
END:VEVENT
